            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0242" n="1076" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1076"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10610</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-08T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 8, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6206. For McFadden [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 425. Embassy’s No. 5638, October 30, 9 p.m., your 549. Because of delay
                    involved, we are unable to concur in resolution of Paris conference. All members
                    of Washington conference agree that action of the conference should become
                    effective immediately. Frothingham notified as requested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
